import LeanForest.H0Tables

/-! **The codeword-level tables, checked by the kernel.** The numerators `F(u) = 256^(u+1) f(u)` and
`F2(u) = 256^(u+2) f2(u)` for `u ≤ 40`, generated by `scripts/forest_table.py`. Each list is read as
the digits of one integer in base `packB = 2^340` (`evB`); the numerators lie in `[0, packB)` because
`f(u)` and `f2(u)` are probabilities, so the integer determines the list. The packed sum
`Σ_m D(m) Σ_{u ≤ 40} (K(m) packB)^u` is a geometric sum per grid cell in closed form (`geomN`), so the
kernel does one big-integer product per cell (`fPack`, `f2Pack`) instead of 41 powers. -/

open Finset

namespace LeanForest.Security.H0

variable [Params]

open Concrete

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
attribute [local irreducible] lut codewordCodes

set_option maxRecDepth 1000000
set_option maxHeartbeats 0

